# OpenHardware
#
# This file is ours. In the fork it was upstream's, so the plan documents told
# contributors to put local ignores in .git/info/exclude instead of editing it.
# That constraint is gone with the fork; add ignores here.

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.venv/
venv/

# CMake output for the native core. tools/build_core.py recreates it.
/build/

# --- Fetched, never vendored ----------------------------------------------
# The SingleStepTests 8088 corpus is ~2 GB; tools/get_8088_tests.sh puts it
# here. tests/fixtures/sst8088/ holds the committed eleven-case excerpt and is
# deliberately NOT ignored.
third_party/

# --- PICSimLab ------------------------------------------------------------
# The reference checkout normally lives beside this repository, not inside it
# (see docs/picsimlab-reference.md). These cover the case where someone puts
# it here anyway, so a 89 MB tree of upstream's source cannot be committed by
# accident -- which is the thing this repository was extracted to stop.
/picsimlab/
/picsimlab-reference/

# --- ESP-IDF --------------------------------------------------------------
# The SoC headers webui/boards/esp32c5.py and esp32c6.py cite. Same
# arrangement as above: a sibling checkout (see docs/esp-idf-reference.md),
# with these here so a tree of Espressif's source cannot be committed by
# accident if someone clones it inside instead.
/esp-idf/
/esp-idf-reference/

# --- Claude Code ----------------------------------------------------------
# Installed from Alexyodude/claude-template, not committed per-project.
#
# This project's OWN rules are not in here -- they live in `rules/`, tracked,
# because `tools/rules_meta.py` parses their frontmatter and CI depends on
# them. They were never editor configuration; they are this project's spec.
.claude/

# oh-my-claudecode session state: notepad, plans, logs, per-session dirs.
.omc/

# Playwright MCP scratch output (snapshots, console logs).
.playwright-mcp/

# --- Editors and OS -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# The vendors' own 3D board models, and the meshes tools/import_3d_model.py
# makes from them. **A licence question rather than a size one**, though they
# are 3.3 MB: Seeed's OSHW-XIAO-Series repository is MIT and the board JSONs
# record that, but these arrive from the wiki's file server, which states no
# licence at all. `rules/licence-hygiene.md` §4 says a dependency in a
# directory nobody exempted is a question for a person, not a header to
# rewrite -- so this repository fetches them and does not carry them.
#
# A checkout without them draws the extruded footprint and says so, which is
# the same degradation a board with no published model gets. Run
# `python tools/import_3d_model.py --all` to have them.
webui/static/models/
